      "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.64,
      "end": 14.64,
      "text": "Booking ahead is the biggest one. Cheaper tickets usually go on sale about two or three months out."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 18.64,
      "end": 24.37,
      "text": "Then look into railcards if your country has them. They often cut a third off for a small yearly fee."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 33.57,
      "end": 40.19,
      "text": "There are often cards for people under thirty, for couples, for families, or for anyone travelling regularly. Check what's offered where you live."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 43.4,
      "end": 48.44,
      "text": "Travelling off peak helps a lot. And splitting a journey into two tickets is sometimes cheaper than one."
